                  UNESCO describes Ben Dinh’s preserved layout as a three-level system complete with zigzag communication trenches, disguised firing bunkers, smokeless kitchen ventilation, and narrow defense chokepoints. Certain un-widened demonstration sections measure just <strong>40 cm wide by 73 cm high</strong>.
