                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
                  <li><strong>Ben Dinh showcases tactical resilience:</strong> As a frontline district command, it illustrates how small partisan units survived directly beneath the perimeter of major American military encampments, using hit-and-run tactics and tunnel mobility to withstand sustained bombardment.</li>
                  <li><strong>Ben Duoc illustrates strategic scale:</strong> As the regional headquarters, it reveals how resistance leaders coordinated military operations across the entire Saigon–Gia Dinh sector. The Ben Duoc Memorial Temple provides indispensable historical gravity, connecting physical tunnel relics with the immense human cost of the conflict.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                  If your objective is to absorb the broader landscape—including the memorial temple, war-zone living reconstructions, and shaded forest trails—Ben Duoc offers a vastly richer canvas.
